          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: गरोदर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गरोदर — garodar — \"pregnant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माझी मावशी गरोदर आहे. mājhī māvśī garodar āhe. My aunt is pregnant."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Unchanging; the formal word is गर्भवती."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गरोदर (garodar) is usually traced to two Sanskrit words, garbha, \"womb\", and udara, \"belly\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
